WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.600
In case you've been hiding under a rock, or
if just don't have Twitter -- bless your heart

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.879
-- Kanye West made his return to the platform,
and proceeded to crack the Internet with 7

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.920
dirty words which would put even George Carlin
to shame.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.050
Last Saturday, Kanye tweeted, "I love the
way Candace Owens thinks."

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.610
If you don't know Candace Owens, she is a
black conservative woman, who originally went

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:27.450
under the YouTube moniker "Red Pill Black".

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:32.090
Candace caught fire online around the summer
of 2017, and my interview with her in, which

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.220
we discussed her evolution from a Lefty to
a conservative, is one of the moments that

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.560
really put her on the map.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.760
It was the first time she had been able to
explain herself in her own words in a long

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.780
form conversational setting.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:48.370
I don't want to rehash the whole thing right
now, but Candace is no stranger to controversy,

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:52.550
and you may remember the infamous debate I
had with Candace and Blaire White late last

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.550
year.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:59.210
The whole thing was a debacle, but #SaveDave
trending on Twitter so who am I to complain?

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:04.369
2018 has already been huge year for Candace,
as she was hired as communications director

00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:09.580
for Turning Point USA, the largest conservative
college group in America..Since then she's

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.890
been touring the country with Charlie Kirk
talking to young people, particularly young

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:19.100
black people, as to why they should embrace
the victor mentality rather than the victim

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.210
mentality.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:25.140
This has included directly attacking the Black
Lives Matter movement as well as Democratic

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:30.890
policies which Candace argues has decimated
the black family and community.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.950
Just last week Candace, Charlie and I spoke
at Berkeley, to a wild crowd.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:40.740
I'm proud to say we had agreements and disagreements,
and even though our styles are different...no

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.060
doubt Candace certainly goes for the jugular
more than I do, I always enjoy doing events

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:50.180
with her and seeing her evolve politically...something
I know a bit about myself.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:55.280
She's learning as she goes, and, as she said
to me in our interview, if I had swallowed

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.390
the red pill, she had snorted it.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:03.060
Beyond any of the politics though, Candace
is a friend and our differences don't define

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.890
us, they actually bring us together.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.780
OK, back to Kanye for a second -- Beyond the
headlines, I don't know a ton about him although

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.300
I'm obviously aware enough to recognize what
an absolutely transcendent cultural figure

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.370
he is.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:19.600
Not only is he hugely successful in the music
world, he has a succesful fashion line and

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.070
is married to Kim Kardashian, who has her
own empire.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:28.470
You may not like the guy for whatever reason,
but make no mistake, he's an absolute mogul.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:34.670
I may not like or even respect the influence
that celebrities have, but Kanye is truly

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:39.650
someone who can truly move peoples minds what
what he raps or what he tweets.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:42.650
This is exactly what happened with his seven
words.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:47.610
Immediately after Kanye's tweets in support
of Candace, the internet went ablaze.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:53.810
Twitter moment's lead story was about Kanye's
support for "far right Candace Owens."

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:58.910
Candace was called anti gay and racist, something
I'm still confused about as she's had dinner

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:03.440
with me and my husband at our house, where
her anti gayness never leaked out.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.090
As for racist, there's nothing like white
Lefty's telling a black person who doesn't

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:12.470
think as they demand they do, that the black
person is the actual racist against their

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.599
own race.

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:15.310
Irony is dead folks.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:19.020
On Monday this week, Kanye refused to back
down despite hysterics from the media.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:23.020
He tweeted out a bunch of video by another
former Rubin Report guest, best selling author,

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.830
and Dilbert creator Scott Adams.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:30.260
In essence, these videos were Scott talking
about what a free thinker Kanye was.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:34.090
Next thing you know, the usual suspects like
Buzzfeed, Mediate, The Daily Beast and others

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.870
were labeling Scott Adams far-right.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:42.700
We've seen this script before with anyone
who dare challenge leftist orthodoxy, be it

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:47.239
Candace, Scott, Colin Moriarity, Jordan Peterson,
or even little old me.

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:52.300
When mainstream has moved so far left that
this wide collection of people are all smeared

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:57.660
with the same charges of far right racism
you know that the overton window hasn't just

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.850
shifted, it's shattered.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:04.870
The authors of these pieces aren’t journalists,
they’re activists...or as Candace says,

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:08.099
they aren’t journalists, they’re hitmen.

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:13.030
To recap: we have a new player in Candace,
who is fearlessly saying how she believes

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:18.470
the Democrats have used the black community
for decades and the victimhood mentality of

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:21.089
the Left is the root of the problem.

00:04:21.089 --> 00:04:24.080
This by the way is similar to what plenty
of other conservatives have been saying for

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:29.740
years, and yes, this includes even black conservatives
like my former guests Larry Elder and Thomas

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:30.740
Sowell.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.560
The voices of black conservatives and others
espousing similar ideas has been largely ignored

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:41.599
by the mainstream however, and that is exactly
why everyone is freaking out about Kanye's

00:04:41.599 --> 00:04:42.599
tweets.

00:04:42.599 --> 00:04:47.639
He just gave oxygen to a set of ideas the
Democrats and the mainstream media don't want

00:04:47.639 --> 00:04:48.930
you to hear.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:53.130
And since they've controlled the narrative
for so long they’ve relied on the usual

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:58.969
smears of racism, homophobia and bigotry instead
of strengthening they’re own ideas.

00:04:58.969 --> 00:05:03.069
Your ideas get fat and lazy when you don't
have to work them out because you've owned

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.930
the narrative for so long.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.960
This is where the modern Left finds itself.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:15.240
If Candace's views are far right, then about
40% of the country, if not more, falls in

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.369
that category.

00:05:16.369 --> 00:05:19.409
I do want to address a different, lurking
danger here, however.

00:05:19.409 --> 00:05:23.779
I know Candace and I believe her to be forthright
and passionate as she figures this all out.

00:05:23.779 --> 00:05:27.520
I obviously don't know Kanye, nor any of his
political beliefs.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.050
So we have an interesting match her, where
Candace is now the rocket and Kanye is the

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.249
jet fuel.

00:05:33.249 --> 00:05:37.520
If Candace doesn't do the intellectual work
to really figure out what she believes and

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:43.650
why she believes it, all while under the insane
microscope of the media praying for her to

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:48.460
fail, well then the rocket will be faulty
and this experiment will blow up.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:52.809
What if Kanye says something absolutely crazy
tomorrow, which is not only possible it's

00:05:52.809 --> 00:05:56.990
probable, or something that's counter to everything
else Candace believes.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:00.879
He has been known to stir the pot and I can
only assume that something like that will

00:06:00.879 --> 00:06:03.750
happen, either intentionally or by mistake.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.830
Does her rocket ship run out of fuel in mid
flight?

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.430
Where does that leave this incredible momentum?

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:13.169
Over the past year when I've talked to people
like Eric and Bret Weinstein, Jordan Peterson,

00:06:13.169 --> 00:06:17.270
Ben Shapiro, Larry Elder, Thomas Sowell and
many others, what I'm most impressed by is

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:22.039
how complete their outlook on politics and
more broadly life is.

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:25.889
They don't jump from conclusion to conclusion
depending on the political climate, they try

00:06:25.889 --> 00:06:31.560
to really understand what they fundamentally
think, so that as new issues arise their responses

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.399
are complete rather than conflicted.

00:06:34.399 --> 00:06:38.020
This is something I've really tried to incorporate
into my thinking and something I know so many

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.120
of you are trying to do as well.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:45.129
This will also be Candace's challenge now,
and I think she's up to it, but only she can

00:06:45.129 --> 00:06:47.339
decide that for herself.

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:51.479
It blows my mind that every conversation we
have in this room seems to become more and

00:06:51.479 --> 00:06:53.740
more relevant as time goes by.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:57.909
For all I know we'll have Kanye in the guest
seat soon enough.

00:06:57.909 --> 00:07:03.360
Whether he is just rocket fuel to boost ideas,
or is he the rocket ship that will get us

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.319
to the solutions remains to be seen.

00:07:06.319 --> 00:07:10.900
But make no mistake, the issues around free
speech, political correctness, and the uncomfortable

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:16.610
truths that might be the answers to the questions
surrounding them have just been leveled up.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:19.239
Are the players ready for the next level,
we'll find out...

